# oracle: pair_style meam per-atom energy and per-atom stress (compute pe/atom and stress/atom NULL) on the w107meam_fetibr setup: multi-element hcp Ti crystal with five Fe atoms (Fe-Ti pair b2, nn2 = 1, fully screened hcp Ti reference), displaced by a random 0.05 A so that no stress component vanishes by symmetry (the symmetric crystal has exact zeros that native writes as -0 and the engine as round-off noise); one static evaluation, the per-atom values dumped sorted by id
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native LAMMPS: thermo rows 1.3e-15, final atoms 2.8e-14, the per-atom c_pe and c_st[1..6] dump 1.0e-12 (relative to the largest magnitude of each column; the file compare is 1e-10).
# oracle-inputs: w107meam_fetic_lib.meam w107meam_fetibr.meam
# oracle-files: w258pa_meam.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-10 filerel=1e-10
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
lattice         hcp 2.92
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3 units lattice
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
displace_atoms  all random 0.05 0.05 0.05 4711 units box
set atom 1 type 2
set atom 5 type 2
set atom 9 type 2
set atom 20 type 2
set atom 33 type 2
mass            1 47.880
mass            2 55.847
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * w107meam_fetic_lib.meam Fe Ti w107meam_fetibr.meam Ti Fe
compute         pe all pe/atom
compute         st all stress/atom NULL
thermo_style    custom step pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          1
dump            d all custom 1 w258pa_meam.dump id c_pe c_st[1] c_st[2] c_st[3] c_st[4] c_st[5] c_st[6]
dump_modify     d sort id format float %.15g
run             0
